            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Can you quickly summarize why the code is moved for someone unfamiliar with the code?\n\nMy impression is that you are moving this to avoid repeating the work as `findDbusObjects` recurses due to the retry logic."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Christopher Meis",
                        "email": "christopher.meis@9elements.com",
                        "username": "ChriMarMe"
                    },
                    "message": "That is a correct assumption."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/perform_scan.cpp",
                    "line": 118,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Previous behavior (please forgive any lack of understanding)\n\n`findDbusObjects -> processDbusObjects -> getInterfaces`\n\ndoes\n```\nscan->dbusProbeObjects[instance.path][instance.interface] = resp;\n```\n\nand then that does not get queried anymore in the next retry for the `GetSubTree` call.\n\n`findDbusObjects` has exactly one non-recursive call site in `void scan::PerformScan::run()`.\n\nMoving the battery saving code there makes the `GetSubTree` call be performed with the same arguments each time.\n\n\nWhich may have different results even for the interfaces which were already found.\n\nNow for each interface `processDbusObjects` does the `getInterfaces` does a DBus `GetAll` call.\n\nSo we are potentially doing more DBus calls as result of this change on systems where the retries are used. Is this the correct understanding?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/perform_scan.cpp",
                    "line": 118,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Christopher Meis",
                        "email": "christopher.meis@9elements.com",
                        "username": "ChriMarMe"
                    },
                    "message": "We're doing less, because the asynchronous function \"findDbusObjects\" is not invoked, if the argument 'interfaces' of findDbusObjects is empty. The run-function is called every time a PerformScan object is created. So I simply moved the check before the asynchronous call."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/perform_scan.cpp",
                    "line": 126,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "We may want to keep the `if (interfaces.empty())` check\n\nhere, otherwise it will be duplicated in callers (even if there is *currently* only one caller)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/perform_scan.cpp",
                    "line": 126,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Christopher Meis",
                        "email": "christopher.meis@9elements.com",
                        "username": "ChriMarMe"
                    },
                    "message": "If the interfaces are empty at this point, they probably are already before the invokation of findDbusObjects."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/perform_scan.cpp",
                    "line": 148,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "sidenote: let's not exit here. Exiting won't revive the mapper, right?"
                }
            ],
